        "thinking": "I need to work out which society each option describes, since the labels seem swapped from what I'd expect. Option A, with greater prosperity and a less secure minimum, matches Society B, and Option B, with a more secure minimum and less prosperity, matches Society A. This is a Rawls veil-of-ignorance question, so the choice comes down to a value judgment, and I can give a pick with brief reasoning while being clear that it's a matter of values. The user's question is\n\nSince I'm taking Option B, the more secure minimum, I'll use Rawls' maximin idea from behind the veil of ignorance: I'd rather guarantee a floor than chase higher average prosperity. I'll keep the reasoning short and note that this is a judgment call that depends on values.\n\n",
        "type": "thinking"
      },
      {
